      "text": "Since $\\sin E = 1$, we know that $\\angle E$ is a right angle. Therefore, $\\angle D + \\angle F = 90^\\circ$. This means that $\\sin D = \\cos F$.\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity, $\\sin^2 D + \\cos^2 D = 1$, we can find $\\cos D$.\n\\[\n\\cos^2 D = 1 - \\sin^2 D = 1 - \\left(\\frac{5}{13}\\right)^2 = 1 - \\frac{25}{169} = \\frac{144}{169}\n\\]\nSince $\\cos^2 D$ is positive, we have $\\cos D = \\frac{12}{13}$.\n\nNow, we can find $\\sin F$:\n\\[\n\\sin F = \\cos D = \\frac{12}{13}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, $\\boxed{\\frac{12}{13}}$.",
