      "text": "Since $\\sin E = 1$, we have $\\angle E = 90^\\circ$.\nIn right triangle $DEF$, $\\sin D = \\frac{5}{13}$, which means the length of the opposite side to $\\angle D$ is 5 and the length of the hypotenuse is 13.\nBy the Pythagorean theorem, the length of the adjacent side to $\\angle D$ is $\\sqrt{13^2 - 5^2} = 12$.\nSo, $\\sin D = \\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\frac{5}{13}$.\nTherefore, $\\sin F = \\sin (180^\\circ - D - E) = \\sin (180^\\circ - D - 90^\\circ) = \\sin (D + 90^\\circ) = \\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\frac{12}{13}$.\nSo, $\\sin F = \\boxed{\\frac{12}{13}}$.The answer is: \\frac{12}{13}",
